tem information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable (f62fdbde1) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Intel Corporation; 32.0.101.6737) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-1145G7 @ 2.60GHz (8 threads) - 15.83 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe padding calculation logic used for embedding data alignment in the PCK header in EditorExportPlatform::save_pack() is incorrect. This causes the embedded PCK header data to start from an unaligned position (not a multiple of 8 bytes). In reality, all other alignment handling uses the correct _get_pad() function, and only here is the incorrect direct modulo method used.\n\n##Current Incorrect Logic\n<img width=\"926\" height=\"240\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f22ca66c-ca2b-4f09-ae3c-de562340c504\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a Godot project and export a build with embedded PCK data (for example, a Windows .exe with embedded resources). Analyze the exported binary/file structure to check the embedded PCK portion. Check whether the starting position of the PCK header is a multiple of 8 bytes.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privac